{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/639486-demon-occult-matrix-as-omens","id":639486,"title":"Demon: Occult Matrix as Omens","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-25T15:00:34-07:00","id":639486,"title":"Demon: Occult Matrix as Omens","content":"One of the things I found hardest about trying to get into the Demon mindset is that the game absolutely screams at me to create a charachter with big goals and motives.<br /> <br /> This is spy stories. Either the protagonist is trying to score a blow against the Soviet Union, or they're trying to stop the Soviet Union. However it's also Demon. If I was playing a mortal super spy, I could come up with a goal like &quot;destabilise ISIS&quot; and I could use my knowledge of the real world to come up with sensible things my charachter could do in game to further that goal. Set up weapons deliveries to ISIS' enemies. Assassinate ISIS' leaders etc.<br /> <br /> However with Demon I can come up with big goals - &quot;escape the universe and start my own&quot;, or &quot;destroy the God Machine&quot;, but I have no clue where to start. How does one escape the universe, there's no rules for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> So I was thinking. What would happen if Imperial Mystery's Omens system was ported to Demon. Good idea? Bad Idea? Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T19:39:34-07:00","id":639729,"title":"","content":"Arch-Demon's playing around with Space-Time? It's thematic, at least. Considering some of the reality warping baseline Unchained can do, an Archmaster equivalent should be able to manage something similar with a kind of 101-version of Occult Matrices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T00:18:19-07:00","id":639931,"title":"","content":"It's certainly an interesting idea, but exactly when would the demon gain enough understanding of g-m physics to do that sort of thing?<br /> <br /> And maybe it's just me, but that seems like a big advancement without some intermediate steps.<br /> <br /> After all, as it stands, embeds and exploits are intuitive knowledge, building supernal level occult matrices would require, I would think, pretty much complete understanding of the underpinnings of g-m shenanigans. <br /> <br /> So I would build at least one intermediate step, a demon who knows enough about the underpinnings of g-m physics that new embeds and exploits are just applications of general occult physics knowledge, like a mage or even a dnd wizard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T00:57:18-07:00","id":639947,"title":"","content":"I think you're looking at it the wrong way. I'm not too concerend with what demons could logcially do. I'm wondering if this would improve the game to let Demons use a system like Omens to achieve personal goals along the lines typically seen in spy stories - just in the setting of Demon rather than the setting of international politics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/639486-demon-occult-matrix-as-omens?p=639729#post639729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arch-Demon's playing around with Space-Time? It's thematic, at least. Considering some of the reality warping baseline Unchained can do, an Archmaster equivalent should be able to manage something similar with a kind of 101-version of Occult Matrices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Arch-demons. But every day demons.<br /> <br /> Non-Arch mages are detective stories. You don't need a system like Omens for that. Demons are spy stories; but I think you do need a system like Omens to help create spy story like antics against inhuman targets.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T10:14:53-07:00","id":640410,"title":"","content":"It's the only way I'm going to see it, because this is as much of a leap as cavemen colonizing the moon with stone and mammoth hide spaceships.<br /> <br /> Which would work fine in owod, but in nwod the writers went to a lot of trouble to make things make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 08-26-2015, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T05:42:20-07:00","id":641416,"title":"","content":"&quot;Escape the universe and start my own&quot;<br /> <br /> You could go... 1) Inside the Gauntlet where spirits of flesh exist; 2) Try and reach Farie without being too much thorn away by the Hedge to conquer your own realm in it; 3) Hook yourself into perpetual life-support and live in the Anima Mundi... etc, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> &quot;destroy the God Machine&quot;<br /> <br /> You could start sabotaging local infrastructure, overseeing it, examining it, figuring out the alleged infrastructures that control the intelligence, that administers the God Machine's processes, attempting to set it into a perpetual Dead-lock (only to realize that's already the case...); or attempt to become a living virus to be re-absorbed when they pick you up for spare parts, causing a systematically massive and exponential number of Falls (&quot;This is my flesh, this is my blood.&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T06:14:17-07:00","id":642898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/639486-demon-occult-matrix-as-omens#post639486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things I found hardest about trying to get into the Demon mindset is that the game absolutely screams at me to create a charachter with big goals and motives.</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay, then do it. Agencies are awesome for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is spy stories. Either the protagonist is trying to score a blow against the Soviet Union, or they're trying to stop the Soviet Union. However it's also Demon. If I was playing a mortal super spy, I could come up with a goal like &quot;destabilise ISIS&quot; and I could use my knowledge of the real world to come up with sensible things my charachter could do in game to further that goal. Set up weapons deliveries to ISIS' enemies. Assassinate ISIS' leaders etc. </div> </div> </div> Not sure what the problem is here. Just replace ISIS/ISIL with God Machine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However with Demon I can come up with big goals - &quot;escape the universe and start my own&quot;, or &quot;destroy the God Machine&quot;, but I have no clue where to start. How does one escape the universe, there's no rules for it. </div> </div> </div> We have expanded rules coming in the Storyteller's Guide for achieving various kinds of Hell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I was thinking. What would happen if Imperial Mystery's Omens system was ported to Demon. Good idea? Bad Idea? Thoughts? </div> </div> </div> Well, you kind of already have an Omen system. Its called your Agenda and your Aspirations. You journey through the Interlocks to reach your techgnostic parabel reveals the path to Hell you follow. Not really sure what it would add. All the Omen system does is formalize a plan into some kind of mechanics, but the mechanics aren't that necessary. <br /> <br /> Take Mother Damnation. She's building her Hell by sundering a time shard in Seattle completely separate from the God Machine and the default time line. Once she succeeds, anything might happen, but she'll be completely free. Her goals/Omens? Destroy all Infrastructure and Cultists, create pacts with everyone in town, set up a ring of enforcers to police area. She's well on the way of acomplishing just that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/639486-demon-occult-matrix-as-omens?p=639931#post639931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's certainly an interesting idea, but exactly when would the demon gain enough understanding of g-m physics to do that sort of thing?</div> </div> </div> </div> Starting from character creation. Its all a matter of creating the right Gadgets, Covers, and the like. There's a side bar in the core book - demons already have the power to do almost anything they want. The only problem is the God Machine is stronger, limiting the demon's potential to whatever he can pull off. You really are underestimating what the Unchained can do. A single demon has the theoretical power to control the weather across the entire globe and cause Noah's flood across the planet. The only reason they can't pull it off is because the God Machine would stop them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T06:24:55-07:00","id":642912,"title":"","content":"How to create your own alternative realm - start with a bolthole. Boltholes are what happens when you accidentily create a room or area that doesn't really exist in reality. Find a way to establish that bolthole to exist irregardless of Cover. Force the bolthole to expand somehow. Use abilities to grow life in bolt hole, independant of outside world. Viola. You just created Hell. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}